<title>UK: FORECAST-UK base rates to rise despite vote result.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-UK base rates to rise despite vote result.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK base rates are set for a quarter point rise by mid-1997, whatever the outcome of the general election due by May, analysts polled by Reuters said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A buoyant economy and increasing price pressures will ensure that either a Conservative or a Labour goverment will immediately raise interest rates by at least 25 basis points. Between now and the election no change in base rates, currently at 5.75 percent, is expected.</p>
<p>Twenty-one banks and investment companies provided the forecasts between September 24 and 26. Sixteen predict the election will be held in May and most expect a Labour victory.</p>
